{"name":"Ivory Paper","hex":"#e6deca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ivory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hard white form of dentin which forms the tusks of elephants, walruses and other animals.","A creamy white color, the color of ivory."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of ivory.","Resembling or having the colour of ivory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivory"},{"term":"paper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sheet material typically used for writing on or printing on (or as a non-waterproof container), usually made by draining cellulose fibres from a suspension in water.","Ellipsis of newspaper; anything used as such (such as a newsletter or listing magazine)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of paper.","Insubstantial (from the weakness of common paper)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ivory","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is a hard, white material from the tusks and teeth of animals, that consists mainly of dentin, one of the physical structures of teeth and tusks. The chemical structure of the teeth and tusks of mammals is the same, regardless of the species of origin, but ivory contains structures of mineralized collagen. The trade in certain tusks and teeth other than elephant is well established and widespread; therefore, \"ivory\" can correctly be used to describe any mammalian teeth or tusks of commercial interest which are large enough to be carved or scrimshawed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg/330px-Horn_Louvre_OA4069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory","wikidata":"Q82001"},{"title":"Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Paper is a thin sheet of matted cellulose fibers. Largely derived from lignocellulose, paper is created from a pulp dissolved into a slurry that is drained and dried into sheets. Different types of paper are defined by constituent fiber, paper pulp, sizing, coating, paper size, paper density and grammage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG/330px-Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper","wikidata":"Q11472"},{"title":"Ivory (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ivory is an off-white color named after, and derived from, the material made from the tusks and teeth of certain animals, such as the elephant and the walrus. It has a very slight tint of yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Decorated_ivory.JPG/330px-Decorated_ivory.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory_(color)","wikidata":"Q1358981"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg/500px-Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg/1280px-Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg/500px-Cylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cylindrical ivory casket, Siculo-Arabic, Hunt Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACylindrical_Ivory_Casket.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Vierge_a_l%27Enfant_debout.jpg/500px-Vierge_a_l%27Enfant_debout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Vierge_a_l%27Enfant_debout.jpg/1280px-Vierge_a_l%27Enfant_d